# `C` requires its type parameter to satisfy the constraint `i32`.  A generic
# feature that accepts `C T` must repeat that constraint on `T`; Fuzion does
# not infer it.  `poly` without the constraint is rejected, while `poly_ok` is
# accepted.
counterexample_31_nearly_universal_quantification is

  C(T type : i32, v T) is

  poly(T type, x C T) String => "hello"  # 1. should flag an error: missing constraint on T
  poly_ok(T type : i32, x C T) String => "hello"
